  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1252 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nPresent model agreement continues to trend towards a new upper-\nlevel ridge slowly building into an upper-level high pressure\nsystem across the Western United States Sunday into Monday. With\nthe high building, most models see the Panhandles returning to\nmuch drier conditions with chances of precipitation dropping below\n10 percent for the start of next week. By Tuesday, models do\nsuggest that the high can break wane slightly in favor of a weak\ntrough pushing through. This trough would put us in better\nstandings to see activity coming off the mountains of Eastern New\nMexico late Tuesday and Wednesday. However, current indication\nform the models has them more in favor of lingering dry air\nwinning out resulting in chances of precipitation to be around 10\npercent at best. Regardless this system looks to be short lived\nwith most models seeing the ridge and high pressure build back in\nby Thursday. As for temperatures, a warming trend does look to\nfollow these drier conditions with afternoon highs heating back\ninto the mid to upper 80s by the middle of next week.",
